      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "If $y=-\\frac{5}{{x}^{7}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We first rewrite the function as\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{5}{{x}^{7}}=-5{x}^{-7}.\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the constant multiple and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-5{x}^{-7}) \\\\  & =-5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-7}) \\\\  & =-5\\cdot (-7){x}^{-7-1} \\\\  & =35{x}^{-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{{x}^{8}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
